{:edb/committed true :edb/basis-t 845 :edb/replayed false :edb/tx-hash "fa0624f7b3ed9054bcdcbdabf972326df395a882a465bcebfae139455462a663" :edb/db-before-t 844 :edb/db-after-t 845 :edb/tx-data [[13194139534157 50 #inst "2026-10-06T05:48:49.788Z" 13194139534157 true] [17592186100578 1100 "Find the general solution of the following trigonometric equation:\n\n$\\sin{\\left(4x-90^\\circ\\right)} = -\\dfrac{1}{2}$" 13194139534157 false] [17592186100578 1100 "Find the general solution of the following trigonometric equation: \n\n$$\n\\sin{\\left(4x-90^\\circ\\right)} = -\\dfrac{1}{2}\n$$" 13194139534157 true] [17592186100578 1145 "The general solution to our equation is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n4x - 90^{∘} &= -30^{∘} + 360^{∘}n, \\mid 4x - 90^{∘}|=-150^{∘} + 360^{∘}n\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSolving the two equations above for $x$, we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\begin{bmatrix}4x &= 90^{∘} - 30^{∘} + 360^{∘}n & 4x|= 90^{∘} - 150^{∘} + 360^{∘}n \\\\ 4x|= 60^{∘} + 360^{∘}n & 4x|=-60^{∘} + 360^{∘}n \\\\ x|= 15^{∘} + 90^{∘}n & x|=-15^{∘} + 90^{∘}n\\end{bmatrix}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534157 false] [17592186100578 1145 "The general solution to our equation is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4x-{90}^{∘} & =-{30}^{∘}+{360}^{∘}n, & \\, & \\, & 4x-{90}^{∘} & =-{150}^{∘}+{360}^{∘}n.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSolving the two equations above for $x,$ we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4x & ={90}^{∘}-{30}^{∘}+{360}^{∘}n & \\, & \\, & 4x & ={90}^{∘}-{150}^{∘}+{360}^{∘}n \\\\ 4x & ={60}^{∘}+{360}^{∘}n & \\, & \\, & 4x & =-{60}^{∘}+{360}^{∘}n \\\\ x & ={15}^{∘}+{90}^{∘}n & \\, & \\, & x & =-{15}^{∘}+{90}^{∘}n\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534157 true] [17592186100579 1100 "Find the general solution of the following trigonometric equation:\n\n$$\n\\tan\\left(2x - \\dfrac{\\pi}{4} \\right) =  -1\n$$" 13194139534157 true] [17592186100579 1100 "Find the general solution of the following trigonometric equation:\n$\\tan\\left(2x - \\dfrac{\\pi}{4} \\right) = -1$" 13194139534157 false] [17592186100579 1145 "The general solution to our equation is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n2x - \\frac{π}{4} &= -\\frac{π}{4} + nπ\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSolving the above equation for $x$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n2x &= nπ \\\\\nx &= \\frac{nπ}{2}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534157 false] [17592186100579 1145 "The general solution to our equation is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2x-\\frac{\\pi }{4} & =-\\frac{\\pi }{4}+n\\pi .\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSolving the above equation for $x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2x & =n\\pi  \\\\ x & =\\frac{n\\pi }{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534157 true] [17592186100580 1100 "Find the general solution of the following trigonometric equation:\n\n$$\n\\sec\\left(2x + \\dfrac{\\pi}{2}\\right) = \\sqrt{2}\n$$" 13194139534157 true] [17592186100580 1100 "Find the general solution of the following trigonometric equation:\n$\\sec\\left(2x + \\dfrac{\\pi}{2}\\right) = \\sqrt{2}$" 13194139534157 false] [17592186100580 1145 "First, note that the given equation is equivalent to\n\n$$\n\\cos\\left(2x + \\dfrac{\\pi}{2}\\right) = \\dfrac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general solution to our equation is\n\n$$\n2x + \\dfrac{\\pi}{2} = \\dfrac{\\pi}{4} + 2\\pi n, \\qquad\\qquad 2x + \\dfrac{\\pi}{2} = \\dfrac{7\\pi}{4} + 2\\pi n\n$$\n\nSolving the two equations above for $x$, we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}2x =-\\frac{π}{2} + \\frac{π}{4} + 2πn, & 2x =-\\frac{π}{2} + \\frac{7π}{4} + 2πn \\\\ 2x =-\\frac{π}{4} + 2πn, & 2x = \\frac{5π}{4} + 2πn \\\\ x =-\\frac{π}{8} + πn, & x = \\frac{5π}{8} + πn\\end{bmatrix}\n$$" 13194139534157 false] [17592186100580 1145 "First, note that the given equation is equivalent to\n\n$$\n\\cos\\left(2x + \\dfrac{\\pi}{2}\\right) = \\dfrac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general solution to our equation is\n\n$$\n2x + \\dfrac{\\pi}{2} = \\dfrac{\\pi}{4} + 2\\pi n, \\qquad\\qquad 2x + \\dfrac{\\pi}{2} = \\dfrac{7\\pi}{4} + 2\\pi n.\n$$\n\nSolving the two equations above for $x,$ we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2x=-\\frac{\\pi }{2}+\\frac{\\pi }{4}+2\\pi n, & \\, & \\, & 2x=-\\frac{\\pi }{2}+\\frac{7\\pi }{4}+2\\pi n \\\\ 2x=-\\frac{\\pi }{4}+2\\pi n, & \\, & \\, & 2x=\\frac{5\\pi }{4}+2\\pi n \\\\ x=-\\frac{\\pi }{8}+\\pi n, & \\, & \\, & x=\\frac{5\\pi }{8}+\\pi n\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534157 true] [17592186100707 1100 "Find the general solution of the following trigonometric equation:\n\n$$\n\\cos \\left(6x + 75^\\circ \\right) = -\\dfrac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\n$$" 13194139534157 true] [17592186100707 1100 "Find the general solution of the following trigonometric equation:\n$\\cos \\left(6x + 75^\\circ \\right) = -\\dfrac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}$" 13194139534157 false] [17592186100707 1145 "The general solution to our equation is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n6x + 75^{∘} &= 135^{∘} + n \\cdot 360^{∘}, \\mid 6x + 75^{∘}|= 225^{∘} + n \\cdot 360^{∘}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSolving the two equations above for $x$, we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\begin{bmatrix}6x &= 60^{∘} + n \\cdot 360^{∘} & 6x|= 150^{∘} + n \\cdot 360^{∘} \\\\ x|= 10^{∘} + n \\cdot 60^{∘} & x|= 25^{∘} + n \\cdot 60^{∘}\\end{bmatrix}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534157 false] [17592186100707 1145 "The general solution to our equation is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}6x+{75}^{∘} & ={135}^{∘}+n\\cdot {360}^{∘}, & \\, & \\, & 6x+{75}^{∘} & ={225}^{∘}+n\\cdot {360}^{∘}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSolving the two equations above for $x,$ we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}6x & ={60}^{∘}+n\\cdot {360}^{∘} & \\, & \\, & 6x & ={150}^{∘}+n\\cdot {360}^{∘} \\\\ x & ={10}^{∘}+n\\cdot {60}^{∘} & \\, & \\, & x & ={25}^{∘}+n\\cdot {60}^{∘}\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534157 true] [17592186100755 1020 #edb/ref 17592186279330 13194139534157 true] [17592186100755 1020 #edb/ref 17592186279344 13194139534157 true] [17592186100755 1020 #edb/ref 17592186279347 13194139534157 true] [17592186100755 1020 #edb/ref 17592186279377 13194139534157 true] [17592186100755 1020 #edb/ref 17592186279388 13194139534157 true] [17592186100756 1020 #edb/ref 17592186279309 13194139534157 true] [17592186100756 1020 #edb/ref 17592186279360 13194139534157 true] [17592186100756 1020 #edb/ref 17592186279364 13194139534157 true] [17592186100756 1020 #edb/ref 17592186279368 13194139534157 true] [17592186100756 1020 #edb/ref 17592186279381 13194139534157 true] [17592186100757 1020 #edb/ref 17592186279316 13194139534157 true] [17592186100757 1020 #edb/ref 17592186279323 13194139534157 true] [17592186100757 1020 #edb/ref 17592186279371 13194139534157 true] [17592186100867 1020 #edb/ref 17592186279337 13194139534157 true] [17592186100867 1020 #edb/ref 17592186279350 13194139534157 true] [17592186100867 1020 #edb/ref 17592186279353 13194139534157 true] [17592186100867 1020 #edb/ref 17592186279356 13194139534157 true] [17592186100867 1020 #edb/ref 17592186279374 13194139534157 true] [17592186101320 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139534157 true] [17592186101320 1100 "Consider the following trigonometric equation:\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sec}⁡(\\frac{x}{4}+{20}^{∘})=2.\n$$\n\nThe general solution of this equation is\n\n$$\nx={a}^{∘}+1\\,{440}^{∘}\\cdot n,\\,x=1\\,{120}^{∘}+1\\,{440}^{∘}\\cdot n,\n$$\n\nwhere $n$ is any integer. Which of the following could be the value of $a?$" 13194139534157 true] [17592186101320 1100 "Consider the following trigonometric equation:\n\n$\\sec (\\frac{x}{4} + 20^{∘}) = 2$.\nThe general solution of this equation is\n$x = a^{∘} + 1440^{∘} \\cdot n, x = 1120^{∘} + 1440^{∘} \\cdot n$,\nwhere $n$ is any integer. Which of the following could be the value of $a$?" 13194139534157 false] [17592186101320 1145 "First, note that the given equation is equivalent to\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{x}{4}+{20}^{∘})=\\frac{1}{2}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general solution to our equation is\n\n$$\n\\frac{x}{4}+{20}^{∘}={60}^{∘}+{360}^{∘}\\cdot n,\\,\\frac{x}{4}+{20}^{∘}={300}^{∘}+{360}^{∘}\\cdot n.\n$$\n\nSolving the two equations above for $x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{x}{4}=-{20}^{∘}+{60}^{∘}+{360}^{∘}\\cdot n, & \\,\\frac{x}{4}=-{20}^{∘}+{300}^{∘}+{360}^{∘}\\cdot n \\\\ \\frac{x}{4}={40}^{∘}+{360}^{∘}\\cdot n, & \\,\\frac{x}{4}={280}^{∘}+{360}^{∘}\\cdot n \\\\ x={160}^{∘}+1\\,{440}^{∘}\\cdot n, & \\,x=1\\,{120}^{∘}+1\\,{440}^{∘}\\cdot n.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have that $a=160.$" 13194139534157 true] [17592186101321 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139534157 true] [17592186101321 1100 "Consider the following trigonometric  equation:\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{csc}⁡2x=-2\n$$\n\nThe general solution of this equation can be expressed as \n\n$$\nx=a+\\pi n,\\,x=\\frac{11\\pi }{12}+\\pi n,\n$$\n\nwhere $n$ is any integer. Which of the following could be the value of $a?$" 13194139534157 true] [17592186101321 1100 "Consider the following trigonometric equation:\n\n$\\csc 2x =-2$\n\nThe general solution of this equation can be expressed as\n$x = a + πn, x = \\frac{11π}{12} + πn$,\nwhere $n$ is any integer. Which of the following could be the value of $a$?" 13194139534157 false] [17592186101321 1145 "First, note that the given equation is equivalent to\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x=-\\frac{1}{2}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general solution to our equation is\n\n$$\n2x=\\frac{7\\pi }{6}+2n\\pi ,\\,x=\\frac{11\\pi }{6}+2\\pi n.\n$$\n\nSolving the two equations above for $x,$ we get:\n\n$$\nx=\\frac{7\\pi }{12}+n\\pi ,\\,x=\\frac{11\\pi }{12}+n\\pi \\,\\,\n$$\n\nSo, we have that $a=\\frac{7\\pi }{12}.$" 13194139534157 true] [17592186279309 1017 #edb/ref 17592186279310 13194139534157 true] [17592186279309 1089 "q-121064" 13194139534157 true] [17592186279309 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139534157 true] [17592186279309 1100 "Consider the following trigonometric equation: \n\n$$\n\\operatorname{tan}⁡(3x)=-\\sqrt{3}\n$$\n\nThe general solution of this equation can be expressed as \n\n$$\nx=a\\pi +\\frac{n\\pi }{3},\n$$\n\n \nwhere $n$ is any integer. What could be the value of $a?$" 13194139534157 true] [17592186279309 1113 #uuid "b76b907c-4182-5eef-ac99-2d356340ad89" 13194139534157 true] [17592186279309 1145 "The general solution to our equation is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3x & =-\\frac{\\pi }{3}+n\\pi .\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSolving the above equation for $x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3x & =-\\frac{\\pi }{3}+n\\pi  \\\\ x & =-\\frac{\\pi }{9}+\\frac{n\\pi }{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have that $a=-\\frac{1}{9}.$" 13194139534157 true] [17592186279310 1000 #edb/ref 17592186279311 13194139534157 true] [17592186279310 1000 #edb/ref 17592186279312 13194139534157 true] [17592186279310 1000 #edb/ref 17592186279313 13194139534157 true] [17592186279310 1000 #edb/ref 17592186279314 13194139534157 true] [17592186279310 1000 #edb/ref 17592186279315 13194139534157 true] [17592186279310 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534157 true] [17592186279310 1041 "selection" 13194139534157 true] [17592186279310 1104 #edb/ref 17592186279315 13194139534157 true] [17592186279310 1110 #uuid "349bcaa5-674e-50d6-beab-5215985552c1" 13194139534157 true] [17592186279311 1034 "-\\frac{2}{3}" 13194139534157 true] [17592186279311 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534157 true] [17592186279311 1111 #uuid "d4eac346-ac15-5c4d-9a98-d37ff9fca2b7" 13194139534157 true] [17592186279312 1034 "-\\frac{1}{3}" 13194139534157 true] [17592186279312 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534157 true] [17592186279312 1111 #uuid "07130973-fe51-567d-aefd-749ce7d301d2" 13194139534157 true] [17592186279313 1034 "-\\frac{2}{9}" 13194139534157 true] [17592186279313 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534157 true] [17592186279313 1111 #uuid "45a4beb0-ea67-5646-9d68-45fcfebf527c" 13194139534157 true] [17592186279314 1034 "-\\frac{5}{9}" 13194139534157 true] [17592186279314 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534157 true] [17592186279314 1111 #uuid "17d84f83-880b-5c5f-ae0c-b5350fd04a40" 13194139534157 true] [17592186279315 1034 "-\\frac{1}{9}" 13194139534157 true] [17592186279315 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534157 true] [17592186