 1017 #edb/ref 17592186279375 13194139534157 true] [17592186279374 1089 "q-330218" 13194139534157 true] [17592186279374 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139534157 true] [17592186279374 1100 "Consider the following trigonometric equation: \n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x+{120}^{∘})=\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}\n$$\n\n  \n\nThe general solution of this equation can be expressed as\n\n$$\nx=-{45}^{∘}+{180}^{∘}\\cdot n,\\,x=a+{180}^{∘}\\cdot n,\n$$\n\nwhere $n$ is any integer. Find a possible value of $a$ in the range $[{0}^{∘},{180}^{∘}).$\n\n$a=$\n{{field-1}}${}^{∘}$" 13194139534157 true] [17592186279374 1113 #uuid "f8fdd777-5df8-5c21-87ef-46d12c5520f5" 13194139534157 true] [17592186279374 1145 "The general solution to our equation is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2x+{120}^{∘} & ={30}^{∘}+{360}^{∘}\\cdot n, & \\, & \\, & 2x+{120}^{∘} & ={330}^{∘}+{360}^{∘}\\cdot n.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSolving the two equations above for $x,$ we get:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2x & ={30}^{∘}-{120}^{∘}+{360}^{∘}\\cdot n & \\, & \\, & 2x & ={330}^{∘}-{120}^{∘}+{360}^{∘}\\cdot n \\\\ 2x & =-{90}^{∘}+{360}^{∘}\\cdot n & \\, & \\, & 2x & ={210}^{∘}+{360}^{∘}\\cdot n \\\\ x & =-{45}^{∘}+{180}^{∘}\\cdot n & \\, & \\, & x & ={105}^{∘}+{180}^{∘}\\cdot n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have that $a={105}^{∘}.$" 13194139534157 true] [17592186279375 1000 #edb/ref 17592186279376 13194139534157 true] [17592186279375 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139534157 true] [17592186279375 1041 "field-1" 13194139534157 true] [17592186279375 1104 #edb/ref 17592186279376 13194139534157 true] [17592186279375 1110 #uuid "40693c9f-68a2-5c18-9307-28072c764274" 13194139534157 true] [17592186279376 1034 "105" 13194139534157 true] [17592186279376 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534157 true] [17592186279376 1111 #uuid "cc05165d-ad81-500b-b846-1dc45f03a177" 13194139534157 true] [17592186279377 1017 #edb/ref 17592186279378 13194139534157 true] [17592186279377 1089 "q-331954" 13194139534157 true] [17592186279377 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139534157 true] [17592186279377 1100 "Consider the following trigonometric equation: \n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5x-{45}^{∘})=\\frac{1}{2}\n$$\n\n  \n\nThe general solution of this equation can be expressed as\n\n$$\nx={15}^{∘}+{72}^{∘}\\cdot n,\\,x=b+{72}^{∘}\\cdot n,\n$$\n\nwhere $n$ is any integer. Find a possible value of $b$ in the range $[{0}^{∘},{72}^{∘}).$\n\n$b=$\n{{field-1}}${}^{∘}$" 13194139534157 true] [17592186279377 1113 #uuid "98a70c61-b70c-50f6-869d-66013f377908" 13194139534157 true] [17592186279377 1145 "The general solution to our equation is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5x-{45}^{∘} & ={30}^{∘}+{360}^{∘}\\cdot n, & \\, & \\, & 5x-{45}^{∘} & ={150}^{∘}+{360}^{∘}\\cdot n.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSolving the two equations above for $x,$ we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5x & ={30}^{∘}+{45}^{∘}+{360}^{∘}\\cdot n & \\, & \\, & 5x & ={150}^{∘}+{45}^{∘}+{360}^{∘}\\cdot n \\\\ 5x & ={75}^{∘}+{360}^{∘}\\cdot n & \\, & \\, & 5x & ={195}^{∘}+{360}^{∘}\\cdot n \\\\ x & ={15}^{∘}+{72}^{∘}\\cdot n & \\, & \\, & x & ={39}^{∘}+{72}^{∘}\\cdot n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have that $b={39}^{∘}.$" 13194139534157 true] [17592186279378 1000 #edb/ref 17592186279379 13194139534157 true] [17592186279378 1000 #edb/ref 17592186279380 13194139534157 true] [17592186279378 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139534157 true] [17592186279378 1041 "field-1" 13194139534157 true] [17592186279378 1104 #edb/ref 17592186279380 13194139534157 true] [17592186279378 1110 #uuid "46a10090-99e8-5dbe-8438-8f682dc56fe8" 13194139534157 true] [17592186279379 1034 "30" 13194139534157 true] [17592186279379 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534157 true] [17592186279379 1111 #uuid "eb19f87d-1e4d-5313-ae6f-2ecb7fa8b53a" 13194139534157 true] [17592186279380 1034 "39" 13194139534157 true] [17592186279380 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534157 true] [17592186279380 1111 #uuid "f0b615d0-81b8-5c45-b243-fae76c4c682f" 13194139534157 true] [17592186279381 1017 #edb/ref 17592